{"name":"Blue Fir","hex":"#51645f","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"fir","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Firan."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A conifer of the genus Abies.","Any pinaceous conifer of related genera, especially a Douglas fir (Pseudotsuga) or a Scots pine (Pinus sylvestris)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fir"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fir","blocks":[{"text":"Firs are coniferous trees belonging to the genus Abies in the family Pinaceae. There are approximately 48–65 extant species, found on mountains throughout much of North and Central America, Eurasia, and North Africa. The genus is most closely related to Keteleeria, a small genus confined to eastern Asia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Abies_koreana_%28szyszki%29.JPG/330px-Abies_koreana_%28szyszki%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fir","wikidata":"Q25350"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Abies_alba_PID1015-3.jpg/120px-Abies_alba_PID1015-3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Abies_alba_PID1015-3.jpg/250px-Abies_alba_PID1015-3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Abies_alba_PID1015-3.jpg/120px-Abies_alba_PID1015-3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAbies_alba_PID1015-3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Abies_grandis_5359.JPG/120px-Abies_grandis_5359.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Abies_grandis_5359.JPG/250px-Abies_grandis_5359.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Abies_grandis_5359.JPG/120px-Abies_grandis_5359.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAbies_grandis_5359.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Punta_de_rama_pinsapo_%28Abies_pinsapo%29_%288620598021%29.jpg/120px-Punta_de_rama_pinsapo_%28Abies_pinsapo%29_%288620598021%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, ht